From 5cb826d982d4d1a0df0facba34fb3e26635d5d9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lu-Fi <lutz@fiebach.de>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:47:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ipu: add a T31 IPU module providing /dev/ipu for the OpenIMP
 OSD blend

OpenIMP's T31 OSD blends overlays through /dev/ipu with one ioctl,
IPU_START (_IO('I', 106)) and a parameter block. On the vendor 3.10
kernel this is the built-in jz_ipu_v13 driver; mainline-based kernels
have none, so OpenIMP disabled the IPU OSD backend there.

Port jz_ipu_v13 (GPL, incl. the thingino wedge mitigation) as
driver/ipu/t31_ipu.ko: DT match ingenic,t31-ipu (reg 0x13080000/0x8000,
INTC 6, clocks ipu + ahb1), clk_prepare_enable, reinit_completion,
void remove/misc_deregister on newer kernels, BUF_FLUSH_CACHE a no-op
where dma_cache_sync() is gone (OpenIMP does not use it), and the
vendor ahb1 clk_get error check fixed.

Tested on a Wuuk Y0510 (T31X) with thingino kernel 7.3.3 by runtime
insmod: /dev/ipu (misc), IPU IRQ counting (~19/s), OpenIMP keeps the
IPU OSD backend, OSD visible in the snapshot, no IPU_START errors.
Not yet: package build/autoload, 3.10 (vendor built-in owns the name
there), soak. Refs Lu-Fi/openimp#257.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
